@@ -0,0 +1,190 @@
+# Repository audit — `ay23-byte/ai-studio-automation`
+
+Date: 2026-11-10 · Audit commit: `9341d56` (merge of PR #138) · Branch:
+`fix/audit-longform-and-channel-identity`
+
+Scope inspected: 22 GitHub Actions workflows, 155 Python modules, 73 test files,
+`requirements.txt`, `env.example`, `.env.example`, `.gitignore`, `db/`, `assets/`,
+the dashboard, upload code and every prompt/description string that mentions a
+channel name.
+
+How this audit was produced:
+
+* every workflow parsed with a YAML parser (one is invalid — see B1);
+* `python -m compileall` over all Python sources — clean;
+* `python -m unittest discover -s tests` — **340 tests, OK (5 skipped)**;
+* workflow-run history and job/step statuses read through the GitHub API;
+* repository-wide scans for credentials, paid providers and channel names.
+
+Limitation: raw job logs and artifacts are served from a host this environment
+cannot reach, so failures are diagnosed from step-level status, commit history
+and the workflow source itself. Claims that require the Windows runner are
+marked as unverified.
+
+---
+
+## A. Working features (verified)
+
+| Area | Evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| Unit/contract test suite | 340 tests pass locally; `validate` workflow is green on `main` (run 42816757724) |
+| CI validation | `.github/workflows/validate.yml`: compileall + unittest on every PR |
+| Shorts production | `make-shorts` schedule succeeded (run 42809182381) |
+| News research queue | `Daily news Shorts — research queue` succeeded on schedule |
+| Editorial approval gate | `core/editorial_review.py:310` raises unless every shot is approved and source-reviewed; `core/news_short_production.py:20` requires `approved_for_production` plus a separate approval record |
+| Upload safety | `core/uploader.py:59` defaults to private/unlisted; `find_private_video_by_marker` refuses a second upload when an existing private copy carries the same run marker |
+| Zero-paid policy | `core/muapi_video.py` always returns false; tests assert MuAPI/Replicate refusal; no paid provider is reachable from production code |
+| Presenter honesty | README states `still_cpu` is not lip-sync and that Hindi mouth shapes are approximate |
+| Secrets hygiene | Regex scan for Google/GitHub/OpenAI-style keys found nothing; `.gitignore` covers `.env`, OAuth tokens and client secrets |
+
+## B. Broken features
+
+### B1. Long-form production has been dead since `b9f0a2d` — **fixed in this PR**
+
+`b9f0a2d` ("Remove paid AI video controls from long-form workflow") deleted 202
+of the 237 lines of `.github/workflows/make_longform.yml` instead of removing the
+MuAPI input and environment block. The file now ends at
+`default: video_first`, so it contains no `jobs:` section.
+
+Consequences, all reproducible from the API:
+
+* GitHub cannot parse the workflow; every push to `main` reports a failed run
+  literally named `.github/workflows/make_longform.yml`
+  (e.g. 42816755450, 42811110312, 42803513288);
+* those runs have **zero jobs** — the long-form pipeline never starts;
+* manual long-form production from the Actions tab is unavailable.
+
+Fix: restore the last valid file (`b49b52e`) and remove only the paid
+`muapi_video_enabled` input and the `MUAPI_*`/`REPLICATE_*` environment
+variables. The restored job keeps `permissions: contents: read`, its
+concurrency group, its inputs (`topic`, `category`, `minutes`, `upload`,
+`voice_gender`, `presenter_mode`, `visual_mode`) and its steps unchanged.
+
+### B2. OpenVINO LTX-Video job is unverified and still has storage gaps
+
+Run history: three `startup_failure` runs (10:07–10:10), then failures at 10:16,
+10:40 and 10:57, PR #138 merged at 12:33 — **no run of the fixed workflow has
+happened since**. The fix is therefore unproven on the self-hosted Windows
+runner.
+
+Review of PR #138 (67 additions, 24 deletions, one file):
+
+* Correct: drive selection now enumerates all fixed drives and requires 100 GB;
+  `HF_HOME`, `PIP_CACHE_DIR`, `TEMP`/`TMP`, the venv and the export target all
+  move to the selected drive through `$GITHUB_ENV`; the post-install guard
+  requires 60 GB before exporting; `GetPathRoot` + `TrimEnd('\')` yields a valid
+  `DeviceID` for `Win32_LogicalDisk` (the bug fixed in `f48545a`).
+* Gap 1: the legacy cleanup only removes
+  `$RUNNER_TOOL_CACHE\huggingface\hub\models--Lightricks--LTX-Video`. The cache
+  that exhausted C: in the failing run was the default Windows Hugging Face
+  cache (`%USERPROFILE%\.cache\huggingface\hub`), which is not touched — the
+  space may still be missing.
+* Gap 2: the export step retries the full `optimum-cli export` up to four times
+  but never checks whether a valid previous export exists. A cached,
+  already-exported model is re-exported on every run, which is exactly the
+  "don't re-download multi-gigabyte models" rule in the brief. The Hugging Face
+  cache prevents weight re-download, but conversion still re-runs.
+* Gap 3: no checksum/`config.json` validation of an existing export, and no
+  cleanup of stale partial exports before a retry.
+* Gap 4: the requirement is a hard 100 GB on one drive. A runner whose largest
+  drive has 60–99 GB fails even though the stated export needs are smaller; the
+  message is clear, but the threshold is not configurable.
+
+Recommendation before re-running: also clean
+`%USERPROFILE%\.cache\huggingface\hub\models--Lightricks--LTX-Video`, add an
+"already exported" fast path keyed on `model_index.json` plus weights, and make
+the threshold an input defaulting to 100 GB.
+
+### B3. Phantom workflow failures hide real signals
+
+Because of B1, roughly every push to `main` produces a red "workflow" run with
+no jobs. That noise makes the Actions list unusable as a health signal and
+trains the operator to ignore red.
+
+## C. Incomplete features
+
+| Item | State |
+| --- | --- |
+| Dashboard | `dashboard.py` is a local Streamlit app; it is not reachable from the browser without a local machine (the brief requires a GitHub-hosted, no-IDE workflow) |
+| Approval queue | DB column `approved` and dashboard review exist, but no durable, non-local approval UI |
+| Storage preflight | Only the OpenVINO workflow checks free space; long-form, Shorts and news pipelines can still fill a runner |
+| Attribution/licence report | `core/asset_licensing.py` and provenance modules exist; there is no single manifest surfaced on the review page per video |
+| English subtitles by default | Subtitle pipeline supports presets, but default-language enforcement per narration language is not covered by a test |
+
+## D. Duplicate or obsolete implementations
+
+* `env.example` and `.env.example` both exist and disagree (different model
+  defaults and provider lists). This PR keeps both valid but they should be
+  merged into one canonical template.
+* `core/muapi_video.py` is dead production code kept alive only by policy tests.
+  Keep it as an explicit "blocked provider" reference, or delete it and keep the
+  policy tests; do not wire it back in.
+* 22 workflows include several near-duplicate documentary trials
+  (`first-documentary-production-trial`, `live-documentary-production-validation`,
+  `manual-live-documentary-e2e`, `archival-documentary-production-trial`,
+  `chernobyl-documentary-production`). They should be consolidated behind one
+  parameterised workflow.
+
+## E. Paid dependencies violating the zero-cost policy
+
+* Production Python code: none (0 references; policy tests enforce it).
+* Workflows: the long-form workflow carried `MUAPI_*` and `REPLICATE_*`
+  variables until `b9f0a2d`; that change is preserved and completed here.
+* Environment templates advertised `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` as an optional better
+  voice. Removed here — the zero-cost policy allows edge-tts, Chatterbox and the
+  self-hosted Chatterbox HTTP server only.
+
+## F. Missing environment variables
+
+Referenced by production workflows but absent from both templates (added here):
+`COVERR_API_KEY`, `DVIDS_API_KEY`, `EUROPEANA_API_KEY`, `NARA_API_KEY`,
+`NASA_API_KEY`. `CLOUDFLARE_*` is correct in templates; `CF_ACCOUNT_ID` /
+`CF_API_TOKEN` are internal names in `core/config.py`, not user-facing.
+
+## G. Security
+
+| Finding | Severity | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `db/studio.sqlite` is committed despite `.gitignore` saying "never commit user/job state" | Medium | `make_shorts.yml:112` runs `git add -f db/studio.sqlite` and pushes it to `main`, producing "bot: update studio db" commits (e.g. 53704f3). Job titles, paths and upload history live in git forever and every run risks a rebase conflict. Move state to `actions/cache` or an artifact. |
+| Actions referenced by tag (`@v4`, `@v5`), not commit SHA | Medium | Supply-chain risk across all 22 workflows. |
+| `permissions: contents: read` on most workflows | Good | `make_shorts.yml` correctly needs `contents: write` for the DB commit above. |
+| Workflow-dispatch input interpolated into PowerShell | Low | OpenVINO passes the prompt through `env:` and `$env:PROMPT`; no direct interpolation into the command line. Keep this pattern. |
+| Secret scanning / push protection | Unknown | Enable in repository settings; not verifiable from code. |
+| Self-hosted runner exposure | Medium | A public repository with a self-hosted runner is a known risk; require approval for outside contributors and keep the runner non-ephemeral only if trusted. |
+
+## H. Performance and storage bottlenecks
+
+* LTX-Video needs roughly 20–30 GB of downloads plus an INT8 export; the job
+  requires 100 GB free and 360 minutes of timeout on a laptop-class machine.
+* The OpenVINO venv is recreated only when missing (good) but pip installs run
+  every time; `PIP_CACHE_DIR` now persists, which helps.
+* Long-form renders 10–15 minute documentaries on a 2-core runner; CPU SadTalker
+  is slower than real time by a wide margin.
+* The database commit step makes every scheduled run a write to `main`.
+
+## I. Features that cannot realistically work on the available hardware
+
+| Feature | Reality | Free alternative |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| LTX-Video on Intel Iris Xe | OpenVINO GPU path is plausible but **unproven** on this runner; CPU fallback is far too slow for minutes of footage | Keep it for short review clips; source real footage for production |
+| SadTalker lip-sync on CPU | Multi-minute talking head takes hours | `talking_avatar` clips recorded in the browser, or `still_cpu` (explicitly not lip-sync) |
+| Chatterbox multilingual on CPU | 2–6× slower than realtime on 4 cores | edge-tts for daily volume; remote GPU via `CHATTERBOX_API_URL` |
+| Cloudflare Workers AI images | Free tier exists but is quota-limited | Pollinations (keyless), Wikimedia/NASA/Archive imagery |
+| Hosted Streamlit dashboard | Free hosting requires an account and a public app; secrets would live there | GitHub Pages read-only status page exported from the DB, approvals via PR labels/issues |
+
+## J. Milestones after this PR
+
+1. **M3 (partly done in this branch)** — OpenVINO cache cleanup/reuse,
+   configurable free-space threshold and the SQLite file removed from git are
+   implemented here. Still open: storage preflight shared by every render
+   workflow, and pinning all Actions to commit SHAs.
+2. **M4** — one free-provider registry with quota tracking and fallback
+   (footage, images, TTS), replacing per-module retry code.
+3. **M5–M7** — research/script quality, footage licensing manifest, AI visuals.
+4. **M8–M10** — presenter/voice, English subtitle sync, render quality gates.
+5. **M11–M12** — browser-visible dashboard/approval and private/unlisted upload
+   with the review package attached.
+6. **M13–M14** — end-to-end production acceptance test and final audit.
+
+Each milestone ships as its own branch and pull request with CI evidence; no
+milestone is marked complete without a run that produced a real artifact.
